Keep the settings.c integer-range assertion at compile time by moving it from
block scope inside a switch case to file scope.

zathura 2026.07.18 asserts, inside a switch case, that gint64 can represent
every unsigned int value before storing an unsigned setting as a signed JSON
integer.  Two limitations of the OHOS SDK toolchain (clang 15,
__STDC_VERSION__ 202000L) make that placement unusable:

  * upstream uses the C23 single-argument static_assert, while the sysroot's
    <assert.h> only maps static_assert to _Static_assert for pre-C23 modes;
  * more fundamentally, clang 15 rejects a static assertion at block scope
    inside a switch case outright ("expected expression"), whether it is
    spelled static_assert or _Static_assert.

Both conditions are compile-time constants, so they do not need block scope at
all: asserting them at file scope preserves the compile-time guarantee on every
supported toolchain.  Deliberately NOT a g_assert(): a release build with
-DG_DISABLE_ASSERT compiles a runtime check away entirely, silently losing the
very invariant the original static_assert enforced.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [portability fix for pre-C23 toolchain]
--- a/girara-gtk/settings.c	2026-10-02 16:54:55.318405492 +0800
+++ b/girara-gtk/settings.c	2026-10-02 16:54:55.335617082 +0800
@@ -12,6 +12,24 @@
 #include <girara/utils.h>
 
 #include "completion.h"
+
+/* gint64 must be able to represent every unsigned int value before an
+ * unsigned setting is stored as a signed JSON integer (see the UINT case
+ * in settings_set_value / the JSON writer below).  Upstream asserts this
+ * at block scope inside a switch case; clang 15 (the OHOS SDK toolchain)
+ * rejects that placement outright ("expected expression") and its
+ * <assert.h> does not provide the C23 single-argument static_assert
+ * either.  Both conditions are compile-time constants, so asserting them
+ * at file scope keeps the check a compile-time guarantee instead of
+ * downgrading it to a runtime one.
+ *
+ * Deliberately NOT g_assert(): -DG_DISABLE_ASSERT would compile that away
+ * in release builds, silently dropping the invariant this assertion
+ * exists to enforce. */
+_Static_assert(sizeof(gint64) >= sizeof(unsigned int),
+               "gint64 must be able to represent every unsigned int value");
+_Static_assert(G_MAXINT64 >= UINT_MAX,
+               "G_MAXINT64 must be at least UINT_MAX");
 #include "session.h"
 #include "internal.h"
 
@@ -230,7 +248,6 @@
     type = "int";
     break;
   case UINT:
-    static_assert(sizeof(gint64) >= sizeof(unsigned int) && G_MAXINT64 >= UINT_MAX);
     json_builder_add_int_value(builder, g_value_get_uint(&setting->value));
     type = "uint";
     break;
